From 81e4da283e10905d27147ba68a03e6146c30ea55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:36:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 54/54] ARM: dts: omap3-n950: keep the eMMC powered across a
 reboot

The MMC core put the eMMC (Hynix, EXT_CSD rev 5, no power-off
notification) to sleep and switched VEMMC off at shutdown. After a
software reset the supply stayed off or came up late, and ubiboot found
no eMMC until the next reset. Keep VEMMC always on, as Harmattan did; the
card is then only asleep (CMD5) and the next kernel's CMD0 resets it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts
index 91ef46b2c..9f4708c55 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts
@@ -739,3 +739,13 @@ &sgx_module {
 	assigned-clocks = <&sgx_fck>;
 	assigned-clock-rates = <195200000>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * Keep the eMMC powered across a reboot. The core powered VEMMC off at
+ * shutdown; after a software reset it then stayed off (or came up late) and
+ * ubiboot found no eMMC until the next reset. With the supply always on the
+ * card is only put to sleep (CMD5), and the next kernel's CMD0 wakes it.
+ */
+&vemmc {
+	regulator-always-on;
+};
